\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Competence and training-pool readout separate the released evaluator from every canonical (clip$=$1.0) checkpoint. (a) Dev-BLEU-4 trajectories on a common step axis: released (orange) reaches 13.38 at step 1{,}820 of 2{,}828; defective-protocol reconstructions (blue band) plateau at 8--10, the eight seven-correction runs (red band) at 11.6--12.6. (b) Gap vs.\ dev BLEU-4 by family (released star); the $(12.62,13.38)$ interval is unobserved by recipe-constructed checkpoints (the nine fine-tunes there are weight perturbations). (c) Full-pool readout vs.\ dev BLEU-4: canonical checkpoints read out at most 12.1 BLEU; the released evaluator 78.8 (70.7\% EM); the unclipped run 99.98 (99.9\% EM). Families are descriptive; checkpoints are not IID replicates.\relax }}{18}{figure.caption.30}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:competence}{{1}{18}{Competence and training-pool readout separate the released evaluator from every canonical (clip$=$1.0) checkpoint. (a) Dev-BLEU-4 trajectories on a common step axis: released (orange) reaches 13.38 at step 1{,}820 of 2{,}828; defective-protocol reconstructions (blue band) plateau at 8--10, the eight seven-correction runs (red band) at 11.6--12.6. (b) Gap vs.\ dev BLEU-4 by family (released star); the $(12.62,13.38)$ interval is unobserved by recipe-constructed checkpoints (the nine fine-tunes there are weight perturbations). (c) Full-pool readout vs.\ dev BLEU-4: canonical checkpoints read out at most 12.1 BLEU; the released evaluator 78.8 (70.7\% EM); the unclipped run 99.98 (99.9\% EM). Families are descriptive; checkpoints are not IID replicates.\relax }{figure.caption.30}{}}
